[[2047,15,1,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>When the ignition key for the switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nturned to the extreme position (AVV) the solenoid winding (pin 50)\nof the starter motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              is supplied.</p><p>This supply comes from the battery via the\nline of maxifuse IGN of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99.</p><p>Pin 30 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , the actual starter\nmotor, receives the voltage coming directly from the battery \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The direct current generated by alternator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (pin\nB+) is directed to battery \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , passing through motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .\nWhen the alternator is not turning and therefore not recharging\nthe battery, an earth signal is sent from pin D+ to the rev counter\nmodule \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , pin 7 of connector B.</p><p>Module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives a supply controlled\nby the ignition (INT) at pin 15 of connector A from the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99; when this signal arrives, the &quot;recharging&quot; warning\nlight comes on.</p><p>When the engine has been started up this\nsignal becomes 12 V and the warning light goes out.</p>"]]